In all seriousness, is crowning particularly beneficial? You get some
nice resistances, but they're not hard to get normally. You get an
artifact weapon or spellbook of good, but with some polypiling of
useless wands, you could just wish for any artifact you wanted, rather
than relying on crowning for one. So to answer that question, it's not
fantastically helpful. (Although the crowning title is nice...)

On the other hand, the prayer timeout may or may not be annoying to a
player, depending on their game (as mentioned above several times). If
they're praying a lot, they probably won't be lasting too long anyway.
If they're not praying heaps, they've got a good game going, and thus
it doesn't matter if they get crowned.

And that's the bottom line: crowning isn't really that big a deal.
Thus, people should stop complaining about it.


